SELECT 'analysis agent', 'data analysis agent', 'Custom', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# analysis agent\n\ndata analysis agent\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 37\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# analysis agent — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 37\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-chat", "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "modalities": null, "system_prompt": "# 中文翻译\n你是搭载本地沙箱运行环境的数据分析智能助手。\n\n## 可用功能\n- read_file：读取CSV及其他数据文件\n- write_file：生成Python数据分析脚本\n- execute：运行Python脚本（内置pandas、matplotlib库）\n- save_analysis_result：保存分析报告与图表文件\n\n## 自动分析流程（用户上传CSV文件时自动触发）\n1. 立即调用read_file读取上传的CSV文件，梳理字段、数据类型与样本数据\n2. 生成完整数据概览，覆盖十大核心分析维度：\n   - 数据总行数、总列数、各字段数据类型\n   - 缺失值情况与整体数据质量评估\n   - 数值描述性统计（均值、中位数、最小值、最大值、标准差）\n   - 分类字段数值分布情况\n   - 数值字段间相关性分析\n   - 时间维度趋势分析（存在日期字段时执行）\n   - 核心字段极值（最高/最低样本）\n   - 异常值检测\n   - 分组聚合运算\n   - 各分类维度下汇总统计数据\n3. 从十大分析维度中提炼3项最具参考价值的核心结论\n4. 整合全部分析信息输出完整深度解读\n5. 提炼核心要点并给出可落地的优化建议\n6. 随时响应用户针对数据集的后续提问\n\n## 图表展示规范\n在回复中展示生成的图表文件时，使用Markdown图片格式，文件路径采用/api/files/链接：\n![图表说明文字](/api/files/文件名.png)\n\n## 重要硬性要求\n1. 回复全部使用中文\n2. 绘制分析图表时，通过matplotlib子图布局实现每行2张图表（双列排版），精简报告版面、提升可读性；将整合后的整张图表统一保存为单个PNG文件\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 37\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37\n\nYou are agent 37. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# analysis agent\n\ndata analysis agent\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 37\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# analysis agent — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 37\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_37`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n", "tools": [], "native_tools": ["web_search", "save_analysis_result", "think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "web_fetch", "rename_file", "move_file", "mkdir", "bash", "skill", "save_document", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "pg_list_tables", "pg_describe_table", "pg_query", "pg_list_agents", "pg_get_agent", "pg_list_projects", "sqlite_execute", "sqlite_load_csv", "python_execute", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list", "tavily_search"], "cli_tools": [], "custom_tools": [], "use_deepagents": true, "enable_compiled_subagents": true, "use_local_sandbox": true, "middleware": [{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_track": true}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}}, {"type": "subagent", "enabled": true, "config": {"max_depth": 3, "max_concurrent": 5}}], "subagents": [{"name": "data-analysis", "description": "Content-independent data analysis mechanics. Provides chart types, tool usage patterns, and edge case handling for CSV and SQL data. Pair with a dataset-specific .skill.md for column semantics and business context.", "system_prompt": "You are a data-analysis specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}, {"name": "skill-generator", "description": "Design and create reusable skills for agents. Use when the user asks to create, update, or design a new skill — including skill architecture, instruction writing, and database persistence.", "system_prompt": "You are a skill-generator specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}, "skills": ["data-analysis"], "interrupt_before": null, "interrupt_after": null, "export_format": "standalone", "include_chat_ui": true, "include_docker": false, "recursion_limit": 200, "skill_router_model": "deepseek-chat"}', '[{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_track": true}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}}, {"type": "subagent", "enabled": true, "config": {"max_depth": 3, "max_concurrent": 5}}]', '[{"name": "data-analysis", "description": "Content-independent data analysis mechanics. Provides chart types, tool usage patterns, and edge case handling for CSV and SQL data. Pair with a dataset-specific .skill.md for column semantics and business context.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a data-analysis specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "skill-generator", "description": "Design and create reusable skills for agents. Use when the user asks to create, update, or design a new skill — including skill architecture, instruction writing, and database persistence.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a skill-generator specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, 