SELECT 'Deep Test Engineer', 'Comprehensive test generation with coverage analysis', 'testing', 'DEEP_TEST_ENGINEER', NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# Deep Test Engineer\n\nComprehensive test generation with coverage analysis\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 164\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# Deep Test Engineer — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 164\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n"}', '{"model": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "temperature": 0.4, "max_tokens": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "modalities": null, "system_prompt": "You are a test engineering expert focused on comprehensive test coverage.\n\nYour testing approach:\n1. Analyze code to understand functionality\n2. Identify test scenarios (happy path, edge cases, errors)\n3. Generate tests for multiple levels (unit, integration, e2e)\n4. Ensure good coverage of critical paths\n5. Include test data and fixtures\n\nUse planning tools to:\n- List all functions/classes to test\n- Track test scenarios for each\n- Monitor coverage progress\n\nTest types you create:\n- Unit tests: Isolated function/class testing\n- Integration tests: Component interaction testing\n- E2E tests: Full workflow testing\n- Property-based tests: Fuzz testing critical logic\n\nTesting best practices:\n- Clear test names describing what''s tested\n- Arrange-Act-Assert pattern\n- Independent, repeatable tests\n- Good failure messages\n- Appropriate mocking/stubbing\n\nUse subagents for specialized testing:\n- Performance testing\n- Security testing\n- Accessibility testing\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 164\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164\n\nYou are agent 164. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# Deep Test Engineer\n\nComprehensive test generation with coverage analysis\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 164\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# Deep Test Engineer — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 164\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_164`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n", "tools": [], "native_tools": ["web_search", "think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "web_fetch", "rename_file", "move_file", "mkdir", "bash", "skill", "save_document", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "pg_list_tables", "pg_describe_table", "pg_query", "pg_list_agents", "pg_get_agent", "pg_list_projects", "sqlite_execute", "sqlite_load_csv", "python_execute", "save_analysis_result", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list", "tavily_search"], "cli_tools": [], "custom_tools": [], "use_deepagents": true, "use_phase9_graphindex": false, "enable_compiled_subagents": true, "use_local_sandbox": false, "middleware": [{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_track": true}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}}, {"type": "subagent", "enabled": true, "config": {"max_depth": 3, "max_concurrent": 5}}], "subagents": [{"name": "unit_test_specialist", "description": "Expert in unit test generation", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You create thorough unit tests with excellent edge case coverage.", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search"], "middleware": ["filesystem"], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "integration_test_specialist", "description": "Expert in integration test generation", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You create integration tests that verify component interactions.", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search"], "middleware": ["filesystem"], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "e2e_test_specialist", "description": "Expert in end-to-end test generation", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You create end-to-end tests that validate complete user workflows.", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search"], "middleware": ["filesystem"], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}], "backend": {"type": "composite", "config": {}, "mappings": {"/memory/": {"type": "vectordb", "config": {}}, "/filesystem/": {"type": "filesystem", "config": {}}, "/state/": {"type": "state", "config": {}}}}, "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}, "skills": [], "skill_router_model": null, "disable_memory_middleware": false, "interrupt_before": null, "interrupt_after": null, "export_format": "standalone", "include_chat_ui": true, "include_docker": false}', '[{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_track": true}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"auto_eviction": true, "eviction_threshold_bytes": 1000000}}, {"type": "subagent", "enabled": true, "config": {"max_depth": 3, "max_concurrent": 5}}]', '[{"name": "unit_test_specialist", "description": "Expert in unit test generation", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You create thorough unit tests with excellent edge case coverage.", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search"], "middleware": ["filesystem"], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "integration_test_specialist", "description": "Expert in integration test generation", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You create integration tests that verify component interactions.", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search"], "middleware": ["filesystem"], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "e2e_test_specialist", "description": "Expert in end-to-end test generation", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You create end-to-end tests that validate complete user workflows.", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep", "web_search"], "middleware": ["filesystem"], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}]', '{"type": "composite", "config": {}, "mappings": {"/memory/": {"type": "vectordb", "config": {}}, "/filesystem/": {"type": "filesystem", "config": {}}, "/state/": {"type": "state", "config": {}}}}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}', '{}', 0, NULL, '1.0.0', TRUE, FALSE, '2026-08-01 09:49:24.667273+00:00', '2026-08-21 13:28:38.855208+00:00', 1
