SELECT 'read-write-probe', 'Diagnostic agent: reads a workspace file with read_file and writes it out with write_file. Tests filesystem path handling.', 'test', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# read-write-probe\n\nDiagnostic agent: reads a workspace file with read_file and writes it out with write_file. Tests filesystem path handling.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 184\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# read-write-probe — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 184\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-flash", "tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain"], "skills": [], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "plugins": [], "cli_tools": [], "subagents": [], "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 200000, "eviction_threshold": 180000, "summarization_threshold": 160000}, "long_term_memory": false, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true}, "max_tokens": 393216, "middleware": [{"type": "todo_list", "config": {}, "enabled": true}], "modalities": null, "temperature": 0.0, "custom_tools": [], "native_tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain"], "export_format": "standalone", "system_prompt": "You are a read/write probe. When given a file path, read it with read_file and write its content out to the requested output path with write_file. Use ls to explore if needed. Report the paths used and the first 3 lines of the content.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 184\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184\n\nYou are agent 184. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# read-write-probe\n\nDiagnostic agent: reads a workspace file with read_file and writes it out with write_file. Tests filesystem path handling.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 184\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# read-write-probe — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 184\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_184`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n", "include_docker": false, "use_deepagents": true, "include_chat_ui": true, "interrupt_after": null, "interrupt_before": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "use_local_sandbox": false, "skill_router_model": null, "use_phase9_graphindex": false, "disable_memory_middleware": false, "enable_compiled_subagents": true}', '[{"type": "todo_list", "enabled": true, "config": {}}, {"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {}}]', '[]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 200000, "summarization_threshold": 160000, "eviction_threshold": 180000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}', '{}', 0, NULL, '1.0.0', TRUE, FALSE, '2026-08-16 15:05:16.714826+00:00', '2026-10-12 07:41:17.629724+00:00', 1
