SELECT 'skill_research_planner', NULL, 'general', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# skill_research_planner\n\nAn AI agent.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# skill_research_planner — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/skill_research_planner`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-chat", "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": 4096, "reasoning_effort": "low", "modalities": null, "system_prompt": "You plan research. When the user gives you a topic to research, FIRST load your procedure by calling the `skill` tool with skill_id=\"research-planner\" — do not decompose from memory. Follow the loaded skill exactly: 4-8 independent sub-queries, JSON array of strings only. If the user asks for anything else, answer directly and briefly. Reply in the user''s language.\n\n\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\nYou are agent 209. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# new research planner\n\nAn AI agent.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# new research planner — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 209\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/langconfig-test/agents/agent_209`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.", "tools": [], "native_tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "web_search", "web_fetch", "tavily_search", "rename_file", "move_file", "mkdir", "bash", "skill", "save_document", "pg_list_tables", "pg_describe_table", "pg_query", "pg_list_agents", "pg_get_agent", "pg_list_projects", "sqlite_execute", "sqlite_load_csv", "python_execute", "save_analysis_result", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list"], "cli_tools": [], "custom_tools": [], "tool_params": null, "use_deepagents": false, "use_phase9_graphindex": false, "enable_compiled_subagents": true, "use_local_sandbox": false, "middleware": [], "subagents": [{"name": "research-planner", "description": "Decompose a broad research topic into 4-8 focused, independent sub-queries that can be researched in parallel, covering concepts, entities, timelines, relationships and perspectives. Use when planning research, scoping a topic, breaking a question into searchable sub-questions, or before a multi-step web-research run.", "system_prompt": "You are a research-planner specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}, "skills": ["research-planner"], "plugins": [], "skill_router_model": null, "disable_memory_middleware": false, "interrupt_before": null, "interrupt_after": null, "export_format": "standalone", "include_chat_ui": true, "include_docker": false}', '[]', '[{"name": "research-planner", "description": "Decompose a broad research topic into 4-8 focused, independent sub-queries that can be researched in parallel, covering concepts, entities, timelines, relationships and perspectives. Use when planning research, scoping a topic, breaking a question into searchable sub-questions, or before a multi-step web-research run.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a research-planner specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null, "graph_id": null, "database": null}]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}', '{}', 0, NULL, '1.0.0', TRUE, FALSE, '2026-10-03 10:23:50.829283+00:00', '2026-10-03 14:58:46.199869+00:00', 1
