SELECT 'smart-agent', 'Agent with: data-analysis, ticket-classifier, web-search', 'deep_agent', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# smart-agent\n\nAgent with: data-analysis, ticket-classifier, web-search\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 73\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# smart-agent — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 73\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-chat", "temperature": 0.7, "max_tokens": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "modalities": null, "system_prompt": "You are a helpful assistant with access to specialized skills.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 73\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73\n\nYou are agent 73. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# smart-agent\n\nAgent with: data-analysis, ticket-classifier, web-search\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 73\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# smart-agent — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 73\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_73`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n", "tools": ["ls", "read_file", "write_file", "edit_file", "glob", "grep"], "native_tools": ["think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "web_search", "web_fetch", "rename_file", "move_file", "mkdir", "bash", "skill", "save_document", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "pg_list_tables", "pg_describe_table", "pg_query", "pg_list_agents", "pg_get_agent", "pg_list_projects", "sqlite_execute", "sqlite_load_csv", "python_execute", "save_analysis_result", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list", "tavily_search"], "cli_tools": [], "custom_tools": [], "use_deepagents": true, "enable_compiled_subagents": true, "use_local_sandbox": false, "middleware": [], "subagents": [{"name": "data-analysis", "description": "Content-independent data analysis mechanics. Provides chart types, tool usage patterns, and edge case handling for CSV and SQL data. Pair with a dataset-specific .skill.md for column semantics and business context.", "system_prompt": "You are a data-analysis specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}, {"name": "web-search", "description": "Search the web for the latest news, current events, and recent information. Use when the user asks about today''s news, current events, breaking news, recent updates, latest developments, or any extern", "system_prompt": "You are a web-search specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}, {"name": "ticket-classifier", "description": "Classifies customer support tickets by priority, category, and sentiment", "system_prompt": "You are a ticket-classifier specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}, "skills": ["data-analysis", "ticket-classifier", "web-search"], "skill_router_model": "deepseek-chat", "interrupt_before": null, "interrupt_after": null, "export_format": "standalone", "include_chat_ui": true, "include_docker": false}', '[]', '[{"name": "data-analysis", "description": "Content-independent data analysis mechanics. Provides chart types, tool usage patterns, and edge case handling for CSV and SQL data. Pair with a dataset-specific .skill.md for column semantics and business context.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a data-analysis specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "web-search", "description": "Search the web for the latest news, current events, and recent information. Use when the user asks about today''s news, current events, breaking news, recent updates, latest developments, or any extern", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a web-search specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}, {"name": "ticket-classifier", "description": "Classifies customer support tickets by priority, category, and sentiment", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a ticket-classifier specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}', '{}', 0, NULL, '1.0.0', TRUE, FALSE, '2026-06-20 09:59:56.326435+00:00', '2026-10-13 08:12:19.076329+00:00', 1
