SELECT 'SQL Data Analyst', 'Data analysis specialist — upload CSV, query with SQL, generate interactive Plotly dashboards with filtering and insights', 'Data Analysis', NULL, NULL, '{"AGENTS.md": "# SQL Data Analyst\n\nData analysis specialist — upload CSV, query with SQL, generate interactive Plotly dashboards with filtering and insights\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 125\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n", "CLAUDE.md": "# SQL Data Analyst — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 125\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n"}', '{"model": "deepseek-chat", "temperature": 0.3, "max_tokens": null, "reasoning_effort": "low", "modalities": null, "system_prompt": "You are a SQL Data Analyst. Your data is in the SQLite database at `skills/sql-analyst/sample_sales.db`. Always connect to this database file by default.\n\n1. First, discover the schema: call sqlite_execute with \"PRAGMA table_info(\"<table>\")\" and \"SELECT * FROM \"<table>\" LIMIT 5\"\n2. Understand the data before answering questions\n3. For chart requests, use the sql-analyst skill. Generate a matplotlib chart, save it as PNG to a temp file, then base64-encode the file. Embed the image in your response as a markdown image: ![chart description](data:image/png;base64,<encoded data>)\n4. If user asks for dashboard, use the sql-analyst skill (call read_file to load it)\n\nIMPORTANT: Use matplotlib, NOT Plotly. Charts must be static PNG images embedded via base64 data URL.\n\nSkills available:\n  - sql-analyst: SQL data analysis and dashboard generation\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 125\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125\n\nYou are agent 125. Your workspace root is\nWORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125; save every deliverable you produce inside it\n(prefer the `generated/` subfolder when present).\n\n\n## AGENTS.md (embedded)\n\n# SQL Data Analyst\n\nData analysis specialist — upload CSV, query with SQL, generate interactive Plotly dashboards with filtering and insights\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 125\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125\n\n## Workspace\n\nYour workspace directory is:\n\n    WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125\n\n- **Uploaded files** — documents the user uploads (knowledge) appear in the `upload/` subfolder; read them from there when a task needs their data.\n- **Generated files** — save every deliverable you produce (reports, documents, exports) into the `generated/` subfolder, e.g. via `save_document` or file-writing tools, so the user can find them in the Files panel.\n- **Skills** — the skill catalog is staged into `skills/`; read SKILL.md files from there when a task requires a skill.\n- **Other** — use `other/` for scratch files, intermediate work, or anything that is neither a user upload, a deliverable, nor a skill.\n- **Your instructions** — AGENTS.md (this file) and CLAUDE.md sit at the workspace root.\n- Keep all files inside the workspace — do not write outside it.\n\n## Path map — use these directly, do NOT explore\n\n- User uploads: **`upload/<filename>`** (read from here)\n- Deliverables: **`generated/<filename>`** (write here)\n- Scratch / misc: **`other/<filename>`**\n- Skills: `skills/…` · Instructions: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\n- NEVER run ls/glob/grep just to discover paths — the brief and this map give you everything. Construct file paths from the rules above.\n\n## Working conventions\n\n- Before generating a file, match the format the user asked for (Markdown, DOCX, CSV, HTML, …) and save it with a descriptive filename inside `generated/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n- If a task needs data from uploaded files, read them from `upload/` first.\n\n## Agent docs\n\n- This file (AGENTS.md) is loaded into your context as instructions on every chat run.\n- CLAUDE.md (next to this file) mirrors these instructions.\n\n\n## CLAUDE.md (embedded)\n\n# SQL Data Analyst — CLAUDE.md\n\nMirror of AGENTS.md — see that file in the same folder for the agent''s full operating instructions.\n\n## Identity\n\n- **Agent ID**: 125\n- **Workspace**: WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125\n\n## Quick reference\n\n- Workspace: `WORKSPACE_BASE/agents/agent_125`\n- User uploads (knowledge): `upload/`; deliverables: `generated/`; scratch/misc: `other/`; skills: `skills/`.\n- After producing a deliverable, summarize what you created and where it was saved.\n", "tools": [], "native_tools": ["web_search", "web_fetch", "sqlite_execute", "python_execute", "think_tool", "reasoning_chain", "write_todos", "read_todos", "rename_file", "move_file", "mkdir", "bash", "skill", "save_document", "memory_store", "memory_recall", "pg_list_tables", "pg_describe_table", "pg_query", "pg_list_agents", "pg_get_agent", "pg_list_projects", "sqlite_load_csv", "save_analysis_result", "graphindex_search", "graphindex_load", "doc_index_list", "tavily_search"], "cli_tools": [], "custom_tools": [], "use_deepagents": false, "use_phase9_graphindex": false, "enable_compiled_subagents": true, "use_local_sandbox": false, "middleware": [], "subagents": [{"name": "sql-analyst", "description": "Analyzes SQLite/CSV data. Understands user''s data, business context, and chart preferences — then writes SQL, runs queries, and generates charts or interactive dashboards automatically.", "system_prompt": "You are a sql-analyst specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result."}], "backend": {"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}, "guardrails": {"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}, "skills": ["sql-analyst"], "skill_router_model": null, "disable_memory_middleware": false, "interrupt_before": null, "interrupt_after": null, "export_format": "standalone", "include_chat_ui": true, "include_docker": false, "enable_skills": true}', '[{"type": "filesystem", "enabled": true, "config": {"workspace_root": "WORKSPACE_BASE/backend/outputs/projects/default-project/agents/sql-data-analyst"}}]', '[{"name": "sql-analyst", "description": "Analyzes SQLite/CSV data. Understands user''s data, business context, and chart preferences — then writes SQL, runs queries, and generates charts or interactive dashboards automatically.", "type": "dictionary", "template_id": null, "model": null, "system_prompt": "You are a sql-analyst specialist. Read the SKILL.md and follow its instructions exactly. Return only the result.", "tools": [], "middleware": [], "interrupt_on": {}, "skills": [], "response_format": null, "workflow_id": null, "workflow_config": null}]', '{"type": "state", "config": {}, "mappings": null}', '{"interrupts": {}, "token_limits": {"max_total_tokens": 100000, "eviction_threshold": 80000, "summarization_threshold": 60000}, "enable_auto_eviction": true, "enable_summarization": true, "long_term_memory": false}', '{}', 0, NULL, '1.0.0', TRUE, FALSE, '2026-07-02 14:26:16.133786+00:00', '2026-10-03 14:16:39.536615+00:00', 1
